comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-15T10:38:13.941Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence 2026-08-15: all-status searches for the exact GitHub issue numbers,run id,platform symptoms,privacy-safe path,stat-matched cache,and timeout lineage found no active item covering this combined run. Closed pm-643e0k,pm-k47yqn,pm-rizqb6,and pm-kpftft are retained as discovered_from predecessors rather than reopened because their recorded fixes remain completed; this item tracks the new regression evidence."
  "2026-08-15T10:41:56.459Z","harness:codex","GitHub linkage evidence 2026-08-15: #1019 https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1019#issuecomment-5301855570, #1020 https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1020#issuecomment-5301855773, and #1021 https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1021#issuecomment-5301855577 each point to this canonical PM item. The three reports remain separate GitHub alerts but share this one regression lineage."
  "2026-08-15T10:56:12.914Z","harness:codex","CodeRabbit review evidence 2026-08-15: finding https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1031#discussion_r3789218620 was valid. Acceptance now enumerates all five conditions separately: macOS projection, both Ubuntu quality predicates, Windows cache omission, and Windows timeout."
  "2026-08-15T19:54:49.590Z","harness:codex","Exact hosted reproduction evidence: Nightly Validation run 31904051790 at branch head 555bf000dfaf14cb29d62dbeda274c5e2ae17aa1 passed Ubuntu Node 22 and Node 25 controls, then isolated macOS canonical workspace alias projection, Ubuntu fresh-clone merge-driver integrity plus nine ignored pm-changelog installation links, and Windows platform-native cache/POSIX chmod expectations. The prior Windows scale timeout did not recur. Remediation preserves all ratchet bounds: canonicalizes real paths before privacy projection, bootstraps clone-local merge drivers, removes only non-reproducible ignored extension-tree links through immutable pm history, and scopes Unix permission tests without weakening portable EACCES/EPERM coverage. Focused local suite: 4 files, 122 tests passed."
  "2026-08-15T20:13:48.189Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: focused Node 24/platform regression suite passed 4 files and 122 tests. Full sandbox coverage passed 504 files and 7,396 tests with exact 100.00% statements (53,572/53,572), branches (39,579/39,579), functions (10,999/10,999), and lines (51,736/51,736). The combined version, changelog, contracts, SDK public-surface, secret scan, ESLint, package artifact, repository static-quality, and dependency audit command completed successfully; npm audit required its configured registry-timeout recovery and reported no known vulnerabilities, while tracker-context-quality remained a nonblocking warning with all enforced bounds green. Manual packed-artifact acceptance in an isolated temporary npm project passed for npx and bunx at 2026.8.15, create/get full unbounded read, history_drift, and storage_integrity. The advisory endpoint separately timed out during the manual npm audit attempt and is recorded as an external availability limitation rather than runtime approval."
  "2026-08-15T20:25:39.413Z","harness:codex","Hosted acceptance complete: Nightly Validation run 31906155419 at exact head 31c14ea031860c1d1f9b0bc8d7da1039571f82e7 concluded success. macOS Node 24, Ubuntu Node 22, Ubuntu Node 24 coverage/static quality, Ubuntu Node 25, and Windows Node 24 all passed. This proves all five incident conditions at a clean hosted checkout without relaxing privacy, tracker-quality, cache-correctness, or timeout ratchets. Run: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/actions/runs/31906155419"
